Use this for an explicit checkpoint or to wait for a selected subset of workers. Pass the exact `run_id` from `list_orchestration_agents` whenever more than one run is tracked or active; agent paths are scoped to a run. Do not build a polling loop around it after a background run: the runtime parks and wakes the parent automatically when the worker run reaches a terminal state.

Only call this after the selected run has been approved and at least one worker is registered. If the run is awaiting approval or already terminal, inspect the native approval/result state instead of waiting.
